        "answer": {
          "short": "$x = -2\\sqrt{2},\\ 2\\sqrt{2}$",
          "worked": "At the $x$-intercepts, $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=(x+2\\sqrt{2})(x-2\\sqrt{2})\\\\x+2\\sqrt{2}&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\\\x-2\\sqrt{2}&=0\\\\x&=-2\\sqrt{2}\\quad\\text{or}\\\\x&=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
